/* HEURISTIC, FROZEN FOR NOW: the SH-4 has a table of its own for FSCA, and
 * its values are not known. Until a source that can be trusted gives them,
 * these are the values Odin always had on the machine its references were
 * made on, where FSCA called the single-precision sin and cos of the C
 * library (glibc on x86-64) on the angle held in a single. Another library
 * gives other last bits, the one of Windows for 1 724 of the 131 072: the
 * same game then drew other display lists there.
 *
 * So that no host library decides: each value is the sine or the cosine in
 * double precision rounded to a single, which the libraries agree on, and
 * the 1 750 values glibc had one unit of the last place away from that are
 * listed below.
 *
 * TO DO: replace all of this by the table of a real SH-4. */

